        "article_text_excerpt": "Belitšev explained that Russia has deliberately relaxed entry requirements and increased the number of flights from countries such as Ethiopia. Egert Belitšev, head of the Estonian Police and Border Guard Board (PPA), has indicated that migration pressure could rise sharply in the coming weeks as migrants attempt to leave Belarus before winter sets in, reports ERR News. Belitšev explained that Russia has deliberately relaxed entry requirements and increased the number of flights from countries such as Ethiopia. Its ally, Belarus, then facilitates the migrants' movement toward Europe. The journey is organized right up to the European Union borders and can cost up to 10,000 euros per person. While Estonia does not share a border with Belarus, Latvia does. Almost all of the 200 migrants detained in Estonia since mid-summer entered the country via Latvia. Estonia has a population of 1.3 million, whereas Ethiopia is home to around 130 million people and hosts nearly a million refugees from ",
